WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.568
We are starting the straighten&nbsp;
up and fly right maneuver,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:00.568 --> 00:00:01.149
where the spacecraft will jettison the&nbsp;
entry balance masses in preparation for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:01.149 --> 00:00:02.055
parachute deploy and to roll over to give&nbsp;
the radar a better look at the ground.

00:00:02.055 --> 00:00:05.760
[inaudible] indicates chute&nbsp;
deploy. The navigation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.240
has confirmed that the&nbsp;
parachute has deployed and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:14.000
we are seeing significant deceleration in&nbsp;
the velocity. Our current velocity is 450&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.840
meters per second at an altitude of about&nbsp;
12 kilometers from the surface of Mars.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:25.840
Heat shield sep. Perseverance has now slowed&nbsp;
to subsonic speeds and the heat shield has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:31.760
separated. This allows both the radar and the&nbsp;
cameras to get their first look at the surface.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.160
Current velocity is 145 meters per&nbsp;
second and an altitude of about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:43.840
10 kilometers - nine and a half&nbsp;
kilometers above the surface.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:01.840
Nav filter converge lastly solution 3.3 meters&nbsp;
per second, altitude 7.4 kilometers. Nav has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:08.080
radar lock on the ground. Current velocity is&nbsp;
about 100 meters per second, 6.6 kilometers off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:14.640
the surface of Mars.&nbsp;
Perseverance is continuing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.800
descend on the parachute.&nbsp;
We are coming up on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.800 --> 00:01:23.680
initialization of terrain relative navigation&nbsp;
and subsequently the priming of the landing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:30.160
engines. Our current velocity is about 90 meters&nbsp;
per second at an altitude of 4.2 kilometers.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:40.000
LVS valid. We have confirmation that the lander&nbsp;
vision system has produced a valid solution&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.640
and part of terrain relative navigation. Priming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:47.600
pba is nominal. We have&nbsp;
priming of the landing engines.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:59.440
Back shell sep. Current velocity is 83 meters&nbsp;
per second at about 2.6 kilometers from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:02.960
surface of Mars. We have confirmation&nbsp;
that the back shell has separated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:08.640
We are currently performing the divert maneuver.&nbsp;
Current velocity is about 75 meters per second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:14.400
at an altitude of about a kilometer off&nbsp;
the surface of Mars. TRN safety bravo.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:21.760
We have completed our terrain relative&nbsp;
navigation. Current speed is about 30&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:26.160
meters per second, altitude of about&nbsp;
300 meters off the surface of Mars.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:32.560
We have started our constant&nbsp;
velocity accordion which means we are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:36.560
conducting the skycrane - about&nbsp;
to conduct the skycrane maneuver.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:40.960
Skycrane maneuver has started.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:53.200
About 20 meters off the surface,&nbsp;
we're getting signals from MRO.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.560 --> 00:03:00.720
Tango delta. Touchdown confirmed.&nbsp;
Perseverance safely on the surface of Mars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:03.840
ready to begin seeking the signs of past life.

